{"name":"Cave Painting","hex":"#aa1100","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cave painting","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The activity of applying pigments to the interior surfaces of caves to create images, especially when carried out in prehistoric times.","The paintings resulting from this activity regarded collectively, especially if prehistoric; cave art;  an individual painting of this type."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cave_painting"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cave Painting","blocks":[{"text":"Cave Painting were an alternative rock band from Brighton, UK, who formed in 2010 and were signed to Third Rock Recordings. They released the singles \"So Calm\", as well as their debut EP, You'll Be Running Soon in 2011, featuring \"Midnight Love\", \"Rio\" and two other songs. They also released a demo of their song \"Leaf\" as a free download on social network sites."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Cave_Painting_Colours_shot.png/330px-Cave_Painting_Colours_shot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_Painting","wikidata":"Q5054913"},{"title":"Cave painting","blocks":[{"text":"In archaeology, cave paintings are a type of parietal art, found on the wall or ceilings of caves. The term usually implies prehistoric origin. Some of these paintings may not have been created by Homo sapiens."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/SantaCruz-CuevaManos-P2210651b.jpg/330px-SantaCruz-CuevaManos-P2210651b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_painting","wikidata":"Q214334"},{"title":"Cave","blocks":[{"text":"Caves and caverns are natural voids under the surface of the Earth and have also been observed in other rocky worlds. Caves often form by the weathering of rock and can extend deep underground. Exogene caves are smaller openings that extend a relatively short distance underground. Caves which extend farther underground than the opening is wide are called endogene caves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Lechuguilla_Cave_Pearlsian_Gulf.jpg/330px-Lechuguilla_Cave_Pearlsian_Gulf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave","wikidata":"Q35509"},{"title":"Painting","blocks":[{"text":"Painting is a visual art, characterized by the practice of applying paint, pigment, color, or other medium to a solid surface. The medium is commonly applied to the base with a brush. Other implements, such as palette knives, sponges, airbrushes, the artist's fingers, or even a dripping technique that uses gravity may be used. One who produces paintings is called a painter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Mona_Lisa%2C_by_Leonardo_da_Vinci%2C_from_C2RMF_retouched.jpg/330px-Mona_Lisa%2C_by_Leonardo_da_Vinci%2C_from_C2RMF_retouched.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Painting","wikidata":"Q11629"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Lubang_Jeriji_Sal%C3%A9h_cave_painting_of_Bull.jpg/500px-Lubang_Jeriji_Sal%C3%A9h_cave_painting_of_Bull.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Lubang_Jeriji_Sal%C3%A9h_cave_painting_of_Bull.jpg/1280px-Lubang_Jeriji_Sal%C3%A9h_cave_painting_of_Bull.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Lubang_Jeriji_Sal%C3%A9h_cave_painting_of_Bull.jpg/500px-Lubang_Jeriji_Sal%C3%A9h_cave_painting_of_Bull.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of the oldest known figurative paintings, a depiction of an unknown bovine, was discovered in the Lubang Jeriji Saléh cave and dated to be more than 40,000 (perhaps as old as 52,000) years old.[5][6]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALubang_Jeriji_Sal%C3%A9h_cave_painting_of_Bull.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Cueva_del_Castillo_interior.jpg/500px-Cueva_del_Castillo_interior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Cueva_del_Castillo_interior.jpg/500px-Cueva_del_Castillo_interior.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Inside of the Cave of El Castillo in Puente Viesgo, Cantabria (Spain). Dating back to 40,000 BC, El Castillo hosts the earliest figurative cave painting in Europe known to date.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACueva_del_Castillo_interior.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Rhinos_Chauvet_Cave.jpg/500px-Rhinos_Chauvet_Cave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Rhinos_Chauvet_Cave.jpg/1280px-Rhinos_Chauvet_Cave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Rhinos_Chauvet_Cave.jpg/500px-Rhinos_Chauvet_Cave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An artistic depiction of a group of rhinoceros was completed in the Chauvet Cave 30,000 to 32,000 years ago.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARhinos_Chauvet_Cave.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Rock_art_bull.jpg/500px-Rock_art_bull.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Rock_art_bull.jpg/500px-Rock_art_bull.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip